<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Mweru</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Mweru is a freshwater lake on the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>, fed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luapula-river">Luapula River</a> and drained northwards by the Luvua into the Congo system. Its shores and the Luapula valley to the south were the heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazembe">Kazembe</a> from the 18th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-livingstone">David Livingstone</a> reached the lake in 1867.</p></div>
